# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE — the hosted side's database
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste real values there. `.env.local` is
# gitignored; this file is tracked, so it must never hold a real project
# URL, key, or credential — placeholders only.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public. Safe to ship to the browser.
# Project ref is an identifier, not a secret — but this file still carries a
# placeholder, because a real value here teaches copy-paste of real values here.
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=your-project-ref
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Public AND RLS-gated. Use this wherever it works: the row level security in
# migrations/20260930113000 revokes `anon` and `authenticated` at the schema
# level, so tenant isolation is then enforced by the database rather than by
# application code — the only place it cannot be forgotten.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Browser copies of the two public identifiers above. The anon key is public
# by design; these two are the only NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars that may exist.
# Mirror both on Netlify.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─── SERVER-ONLY. NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_. ───
#
# A `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variable is inlined into client JavaScript by the bundler.
# There is no runtime check and no warning: the key simply ships to every visitor.
# If you add any Supabase secret here, leave the prefix off.
#
# Server-side use only. Narrow writes the RLS-scoped path cannot make.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─── MANAGEMENT CREDENTIAL — READ BEFORE USING ───
#
# A Supabase personal access token is ACCOUNT-ADMIN: it can read every API key,
# create projects, and drop the database. It is the right credential for running
# migrations and rotating keys, and the wrong one for a Next.js app.
#
# It belongs to the CLI and to CI:
#
#   npx supabase link --project-ref <ref>
#   npx supabase db push                      # with SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN set
#
# and to the supabase-admin tooling — not to anything under src/ or app/.
#
# If this app genuinely needs it, paste it into `.env.local` here, keep it out of
# git, and know what you are holding: full admin over every tenant's data,
# including tenants who have nothing to do with the merchant running this app.
# See TASKS.md § What to push to GitHub and § Supabase.
#
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ─── Signing secret for short-lived agent credentials ───
#
# The name matters: the SDK reads AGENTPORT_SIGNING_SECRET, not
# AGENTPORT_SIGNING_KEY. This file advertised the wrong name and nothing read
# either, so it was a control that looked like a control — the same failure as
# `UserDelegation.scope` in the SDK, and the reason TASKS.md 0.4 existed.
#
# Mint one with the CLI. It is an HMAC key held by the merchant's environment;
# the token issuer and verifier are the only things that need it, and it is
# never written to a config file or a ledger row.
#
#   npx agent-port secret
#
# SERVER-ONLY. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — see the note above.
AGENTPORT_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ─── Console append door key ───
#
# Server-only HMAC key the console uses to append decisions through the
# `agentport_console_append` door (see lib/console-append.ts). The door runs
# SECURITY DEFINER and checks this HMAC itself, so a missing key means rows are
# dropped loudly (`console_append_skipped`), never queued. This is the key the
# door was provisioned with — it is not the signing secret above.
#
# SERVER-ONLY. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
AGENTPORT_CONSOLE_HMAC=

# ─── Hosted governor URL ───
#
# The Rust governor runs on Agent Port's infrastructure, not the merchant's.
# The install package needs this origin to write the discovery manifest and
# execute endpoint. It is not a per-tenant secret and never carries a token.
# Outside local development it must be https.
AGENTPORT_WORKER_URL=https://governor.example.test

# ─── GitHub broker ───
#
# The console holds NO GitHub App private key, OAuth client secret or webhook
# secret. Every GitHub operation — install, list repos, open the install pull
# request, read PR state — is performed by the separately deployed broker
# (`broker/`, built with `npm --prefix broker run build`, served by its own
# systemd unit). The console forwards the caller's Supabase access token plus a
# shared service token over TLS; the broker verifies the caller and membership
# itself.
#
# Both are required for step 04 (connect repo) and step 05 (open install PR).
# With either missing, every GitHub route answers 503 "GitHub broker is not
# configured — this is our side." rather than falling back to a local key path.
#
# GITHUB_BROKER_URL: base URL of the broker, reachable from the console server.
#   In the current deployment Caddy mounts it under the governor origin at
#   a broker mount path such as https://<governor-origin>/github (the broker
#   itself listens on 127.0.0.1:8790). This is not the console origin.
# GITHUB_BROKER_TOKEN: the shared service token the broker expects in
#   `X-AgentPort-Broker-Token`. Must equal the broker's GITHUB_BROKER_TOKEN.
#
# SERVER-ONLY. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — this token is a service credential.
GITHUB_BROKER_URL=
GITHUB_BROKER_TOKEN=

# ─── Local development only ───
#
# Fallback tenant id used by the single-process demo store (lib/store.ts) when
# no Supabase Auth workspace is selected. Never set this in production: real
# tenants are resolved from the authenticated membership, not from an env var.
# AGENTPORT_TENANT=

# ─── Pilot request email ───
#
# /api/contact writes every request to Supabase (`pilot_requests`) and, when
# this key is set, emails the founder through Resend. The row is the record of
# truth: with no key the route still stores the request and reports
# `notified: not_configured`, so a missing mail key never loses a lead.
#
# SERVER-ONLY. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. A mail key in client JavaScript is a
# spam relay on our domain.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults are AgentPort <noreply@relayforge.in> and
# arpit@relayforge.in. Keep the From domain verified in Resend.
# PILOT_NOTIFY_FROM=
# PILOT_NOTIFY_TO=
